      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment. Actual producer: Codex (gpt-6-astra), reconciliation. GMR's source wording is preserved verbatim; no hgm_gloss change. na re owns the opening claim. The authorial mdzad pa is omitted: the source says the commentary was composed by Vinitadeva, whereas makes this statement introduces his quotation. The later gsungs pa/de own statement/this in the opponent's inference. dul ba lhas stays whole, without a detached agentive s. med is a negative existential word at d5, not a standalone particle; it owns not while the English existential frame remains unwrapped. ga la yod owns the complete d3 rhetorical phrase how could there ever be. dbang/gis own forced/through, the causal force and instrumental link to karmic ripening. Despite the positive gang ba/whole glossary, gang ba is omitted here: the source's filled-with-pus relation is distributed in river of pus; C05:290 separately renders whole and full, so whole is not a secure isolated fullness exponent. mi 'thad par is an established negative lexical unit for mistaken. The final single rnag owns the subject pus in the pus is real pus; the predicate repetition is unwrapped. ngo has no separate declarative exponent; subject gyis has no separate word in the active English construction. Other omitted emphasis, copular and reporting material is distributed, not declared absent."
